  "status": "passed",
  "change": "Reuse the post-commit creator services to prepare wiki lists and ManageWiki metadata. A fingerprint receipt and blocking per-wiki handoff lock let the coordinator skip its separate metawiki bootstrap. Invalid receipts retain the existing repair process. The target updater still launches once.",
  "focused_checks": [
    "complete public/private receipts accepted",
    "unsealed, malformed, changed and partial metadata rejected",
    "shared registration and privacy list consistency required",
    "timestamp-only and unrelated wiki changes accepted",
    "SIGTERM interrupts coordinator lock wait and preserves pending work"
  ],
  "benchmark": {
    "method": "12 sequential fresh form creations alternating separate-metadata-process and prepared paths in four batches; six per mode, four public and two private per mode. Both modes use the new post-commit producer; control forces the former unconditional metadata child and candidate validates the receipt. This isolates the redundant bootstrap cost rather than reproducing the entire historical application. Both use the current signal-based process waiter and container-local source. No schema/OAuth tests ran during timings.",
    "limitations": [
      "Small local sample; all outliers retained.",
      "Submit-to-completion uses Redis timestamps; browser verification includes 500 ms observation intervals and API request time. Worker measurements use Redis start/finish timestamps.",
      "Idle sample leaves creation traffic idle for two minutes; ordinary background services remain enabled."
    ],
